Body:
For now you can add the permission check in custom tool itself:
```
export default tool({
  description: "Ask a question",
  args: {
    query: tool.schema.string().describe("Search query")
  },
  async execute(args, ctx) {
    const q = encodeURIComponent(args.query);    
    await ctx.ask({
      permission: "mytoolname",
      patterns: [q],
      always: ["*"],
      metadata: {},
    })

    // at this point permission is already granted
```

To others looking, here's how to pin your OpenRouter provider via `opencode.jsonc`:

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "openrouter": {
      "models": {
        "minimax/minimax-m2.5": {
          "name": "Minimax M2.5 (official)",
          "options": {
            "provider": {
              "only": [
                "minimax/fp8"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

